# 📌 27. Practical Example — Script

Create:

```bash
nano backup.sh
```

Put:

```bash
#!/bin/bash

echo "Starting backup..."
echo "Backup completed."
```

Initially, you may not be able to execute it directly.

Try:

```bash
./backup.sh
```

You may receive:

```text
