# 🔐 35. Cybersecurity Importance

Linux permissions are extremely important in cybersecurity.

Security professionals use them to help protect:

* configuration files
* passwords
* SSH keys
* logs
* databases
* application files
* scripts
* system files
* backups

Incorrect permissions can cause:

```text
Information disclosure
Unauthorized modification
Privilege escalation
Data tampering
